From e0e63cd4263410f31db2d19c9a1e7158ce68203b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:52:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add DPDP-compliant Privacy Policy and consent checkboxes

- Added privacy-policy.html covering: Data Fiduciary identity, what
  personal data is collected via the contact form and Scope
  Estimator wizard, purpose/legal basis (consent), third-party
  sharing disclosure (Google Apps Script/Sheets used to store
  enquiries), retention, cookies, security, Data Principal rights,
  a Grievance Officer contact block, and the right to complain to
  the Data Protection Board of India -- per the DPDP Act 2023, DPDP
  Rules 2025, and IT Act 2000 / SPDI Rules 2011.
- Added a required consent checkbox, linked to the new Privacy
  Policy, to both the main contact form and step 3 of the Scope
  Estimator wizard (both collect name/org/email/phone).
- script.js: validateField() now correctly validates checkboxes
  (previously a checkbox's required state was never actually
  checked, since its .value is always non-empty regardless of
  checked state). Wizard submit handler now blocks submission until
  consent is checked. Consent flag is now included in the data sent
  to the Google Sheet for the main contact form.
- Linked Privacy Policy from the footer on both pages and added it
  to sitemap.xml.
